claimed: acme-ari -- Automated Renewal Information, the second of the three. A CA publishes a SUGGESTED renewal window per certificate (renewalInfo in the directory, GET renewalInfo/<certID>), so that a mass revocation does not become every client renewing at the same minute; a client renews inside that window instead of on its own fixed countdown. The work: the certID (base64url of the Authority Key Identifier's keyIdentifier, a dot, base64url of the serial -- both read out of the leaf's own DER by hand, since the JDK exposes the AKI only as a raw extension), the window parse, and feeding it into `ensure`'s decision BESIDE renewBefore rather than instead of it (a CA that publishes nothing, or nonsense, must not stop a renewal). Tested against Pebble, which serves renewalInfo. Touches Acme.scala, specs/acme.md, docs.
